   "note": "Known mismatch with MDP04 (V5): expiry offsets 8 months (aspirin) and 10 (melatonin) there vs 9 and 11 here; melatonin 90 (3.3) %LC there vs 89.2 here; loperamide 100 (30) there vs 96.3 here. Calibration anchor for the computed layer: the aspirin row (hydrolysis-prone repackaged solid, 550 days in flight) is a measured point the computed layer is calibrated against, so keep it out of any validation set used to judge that layer. Expiry offsets were read through a summary fetch; MDP04 gives 8 months for aspirin and 10 for melatonin. No ground controls. Use: single-point check of repackaged solids at 550 days."
